    "summary": "High‑energy show with debut Bird Song, stellar China>Rider and tight jams",
    "blurb": "The February 19 1971 Capitol Theater concert delivers a smoking China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue, the first live Bird Song, and a powerful Good Lovin' jam. Jerry’s guitar soars, Pigpen’s organ drives the blues‑heavy moments, and the rhythm section stays locked in. Soundboard recordings capture the performance with excellent fidelity.",
    "review": "What unfolds at the Capitol Theater on February 19, 1971 is a snapshot of the Dead in peak form just before Mickey Hart's temporary departure. The first set sparkles from the opening Truckin' through an electric Dark Hollow and builds to a blistering China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider that showcases Jerry’s soaring bends and Bob’s psychedelic‑blues fills. The second set launches with the historic debut of Bird Song, followed by Easy Wind and Deal, each propelled by Pigpen’s gritty organ work. Highlights include a thunderous Smokestack Lightning, a tight The Other One/Wharf Rat stretch, and an inspired Good Lovin' that keeps the crowd breathing fire. Across all sources the show is praised for its high‑energy flow, clean transitions, and a rhythm section that remains rock‑solid despite the lineup shift.",
